@Bill
I was in the middle of a herd of stampeding cows today!  That is in a 'movie.'  We were visiting the Mormon Battalion Historic Site in Old Town San Diego.  You go through a 35 min 'walk' simulating the 2000 mile march of 500+ people in 1846-47.  They were sent to fight the Mexicans, but the war ended before they got to San Diego.  On the way they were 'attacked', but by a thundering herd.  It's called "The Battle of the Bulls".

Interesting place to visit....
